Well it seems it's a bit more complex, here's an example which represents more or less our usecase (nested documents in nested documents [..]).

User.ts
```ts
@Entity()
export class User {

    @ObjectIdColumn()
    id: ObjectID;

    @Column()
    name: string;

    @Column(type => ContactContainer)
    contact: ContactContainer;
}
```

ContactContainer.ts
```ts
@Entity()
export class ContactContainer {

    @ObjectIdColumn()
    id?: string;

    @Column(type => Contact)
    general: Contact;

    @Column(type => Contact)
    otherstuff: Contact;

    @Column(type => Contact)
    moreotherstuff: Contact;
}
```

Contact.ts
```ts
@Entity()
export class Contact {

    @ObjectIdColumn()
    id?: string;

    @Column()
    email: string;

    @Column()
    fax: string;

    @Column()
    phone: string;
}
```

